:name: zephyr-bms on STM32 NUCLEO-H743ZI
:description: Fake BMS firmware (Zephyr) with FDCAN1 on a CAN hub bridged to host SocketCAN

# Usage (from the repo root, see scripts/run-renode.sh):
#   cd <repo root>; renode -e '$bin=@/path/to/zephyr.elf' renode/bms.resc
# Optional variables, set the same way before the script:
#   $can_if   host SocketCAN interface (default vcan0)
#   $uart_log file the firmware's console is copied to

using sysbus

$bin?=@/mnt/yocto/zephyr/build/zephyr/zephyr.elf
$can_if?="vcan0"
$uart_log?=@/tmp/zephyr-bms-uart.log
# Relative paths are looked up from the current directory: run from the repo root.
$repl?=@renode/nucleo_h743zi_bms.repl

# One emulated machine. The H743ZI and H753ZI differ only by a crypto block;
# nucleo_h743zi_bms.repl takes Renode's NUCLEO-H753ZI board file (-> stm32h7.repl,
# where fdcan1 is a CAN.MCAN model and the IWDG a watchdog model) and fixes
# the watchdog clock.
mach create "bms"
machine LoadPlatformDescription $repl

# The firmware's console: shown as a log/analyzer, and copied to a file
# (the test script reads it).
showAnalyzer usart3
usart3 CreateFileBackend $uart_log true

macro reset
"""
    sysbus LoadELF $bin
"""
runMacro $reset

# The CAN wiring: fdcan1 <-> canHub <-> host SocketCAN interface.
# A CANHub is Renode's model of a bus: every frame a node sends is delivered
# to every other node on the hub.
emulation CreateCANHub "canHub"
connector Connect fdcan1 canHub
machine CreateSocketCANBridge "socketcan" $can_if
connector Connect socketcan canHub
